  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "OpenccNetLib v1.3.0\n\n            This release focuses on performance, code simplification, and astral-safe text handling.\n\n            Highlights\n            - 🚀 **Pre-chunked Parallel Conversion**: Balanced `SplitRanges` batching (128–512 ranges per chunk) now feeds `Parallel.For`\n            with evenly sized tasks — achieving >50% faster conversion on S2T workloads (1M chars → ~21 ms on i5-13400).\n            - 🧩 Added `Chunk` struct and `BuildChunks()` helper for predictable, cache-friendly load balancing with per-chunk\n            `StringBuilder` buffers (slightly higher memory usage +3 MB, well worth the speedup).\n            - 🧠 Introduced `StarterUnion` with `UnionKey`-based caching in `ConversionPlanCache` — fewer allocations and faster startup.\n            - ⚙️ Added `BuildFromStarterMasks()` to construct `StarterUnion` directly from precomputed per-starter length masks,\n            eliminating full key scans and saving ~10 ms on large dictionary builds.\n            - 🧮 O(1) per-starter metadata: 64-bit length mask + minLen + cap → skips impossible probe lengths instantly.\n            - 🈚 Astral-safe `GetAt(c0, c1, hasSecond, …)` detects surrogate pairs, clamps `len == 1`, and ensures full non-BMP safety.\n            - 🗜️ Shared high-surrogate (c0) indexing for astral characters (st/ts_characters) → dense, cache-friendly tables.\n            - 🔧 Simplified bit helpers (`LowestLen` / `HighestLen`) using compact inlined loops — faster than `BitOperations` for small masks.\n            - ✅ Corrected longest-match behavior; single-grapheme fast path now triggers only when no longer candidates exist.\n            - 💡 .NET Standard 2.0-compatible throughout — removed “??=”, static locals, and lambda captures for full runtime portability.\n\n            Project: https://github.com/laisuk/OpenccNet",
